// Title: Regedit as Trusted Installer
// Sigma ID: 883835a7-df45-43e4-bf1d-4268768afda4
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Florian Roth (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2021-05-27 | Modified: 2022-10-09
// ATT&CK: privilege-escalation, T1548
// Description: Detects a regedit started with TrustedInstaller privileges or by ProcessHacker.exe
// False positives:
//   - Unlikely
// References:
//   - https://twitter.com/1kwpeter/status/1397816101455765504
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_regedit_trustedinstaller.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, microsoft_xdr schema)

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "\\regedit.exe" and (InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\TrustedInstaller.exe" or InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\ProcessHacker.exe")
